# Market Terminal

## What This Is

A personal, institutional-grade markets system for César that runs mostly unattended on his Windows machine. One data engine (LSEG Workspace plus free public sources) feeds five surfaces: a Bloomberg-style market dashboard, daily and weekly PPTX decks, an Ideas Screener, an IBKR-based portfolio view, and a 13F tracker for large AI and infrastructure funds. Arithmetic is done in code; an LLM (Claude Haiku via `claude -p`) only writes prose around numbers it never invents.

Full requirements: `BRIEF.md`. Data and style rules: `CLAUDE.md`.

## Core Value

Every number César sees is correct and traceable to its source. A surface that shows fewer things but reconciles is worth more than one that shows everything with a silent error.

